\end{equation}\]Exponential function:\[\begin{align}
e^z
&= \sum_{= 1}^n \frac{z^}{!}
  = 1 + z + \frac{z^2}{2!} + \frac{z^3}{3!} + \ldots \quad\text{values $z$}.
\tag{B.8}\\
e^{-z}
&= \sum_{= 1}^n \frac{(-z)^}{!}
  = 1 - z + \frac{z^2}{2!} - \frac{z^3}{3!} + \ldots \quad\text{values $z$}.
\tag{B.9} \\
e
&= \lim_{z\\infty} \left(1 + \frac{1}{z}\right)^z
\tag{B.10}\\
1/e
&= \lim_{z\\infty} \left(1 - \frac{1}{z}\right)^z
\tag{B.11}
\end{align}\]Exponential function:\[\begin{align}
